 at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is/are"},{"id":310528,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Carboxylic Acid Derivatives","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Most Important Selected Qs for JEE Advanced","q":"Which of the following reaction (s) can generate a five membered ring as the major product?","options":["<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-ccce92a986ecd4b5.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-ccce92a986ecd4b5.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-ccce92a986ecd4b5.png\"><br/>","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-8d507541a01cdea6.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8d507541a01cdea6.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8d507541a01cdea6.png\"><br/>","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-2280f08becc4f357.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-2280f08becc4f357.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-2280f08becc4f357.png\"><br/>","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-4f7a8eec009ce688.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-4f7a8eec009ce688.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-4f7a8eec009ce688.png\"><br/>"],"answer":3,"solution":"<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-a4ed9508f577bc84.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a4ed9508f577bc84.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a4ed9508f577bc84.png\"><br/>\n$\\mathrm{I}_2$ will attack the double bond to form a cyclic halonium ion. It then undergoes on intramolecular reaction. Formation of five membered ring is favoured because (i) attack by a nucleophile on a halonium ion normally takes place at the more substituted site.\n(ii) Formation of five membered ring is more probable.<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-3e413695d8853396.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-3e413695d8853396.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-3e413695d8853396.png\"><br/>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Most Important Selected Qs for JEE Advanced","_book":"68f1ce4cc729e5251bd00430","_chapterKey":"68f1ce4cc729e5251bd00430__68f8d4375694d9c689598ed9__68f8d4385694d9c689598edc__68f8d43d5694d9c689598ee1","_marksId":"67c994c1cc180496584ed2ae","question":"Which of the following reaction (s) can generate a five membered ring as the major product?"}]}